# Print-specific overrides. scripts/build.mjs merges these on top of content.env
# and validates the merged values against content.limits.env. The sheet must hold
# exactly ONE A4 page (the build fails on two), and its main column is narrow,
# about 55 characters per line, so everything long is condensed here.

# The PDF links back to the live page instead of offering itself for download.
PAGE_TITLE=Nektarios Zabouris CV
CV_FILENAME=https://geofeid.github.io/zab-cv/
CV_DOWNLOAD_NAME=Nektarios_Zabouris_Online_CV
CV_LABEL=Online CV

# About, cut from ~590 to under 380 characters: the career goal stays, the
# closing "seeking opportunities" sentence goes.
ABOUT_PARAGRAPH=Passionate IT Support Engineer with a strong interest in technology, particularly mobile devices and computers. Skilled in resolving technical challenges, providing prompt user support and quickly adapting to new tools and systems. A fast learner, self-motivated and solution-oriented, aiming to grow in system administration and advanced technical support.

# One paragraph per job. A non-empty EXPn_DESC replaces the numbered
# EXPn_DESC1..n paragraphs in print. Budgets: Adaptit <= 300, iRepair <= 220,
# the three short jobs <= 110 (two print lines each).
EXP5_DESC=Provide Level 1 support to internal users and external clients across multiple environments. Manage Microsoft 365 through the Admin Center. Support IT infrastructure and software deployment for customer projects. Monitor ticketing for timely resolution and client communication.
EXP4_DESC=Repaired mobile phones, tablets and computers across the Nea Erythraia and Maroussi stores. Supervised technicians, planned monthly shifts, and handled technical training, sales, invoices, suppliers and complaints.
EXP3_DESC=Assisted in IT and communication system operations in Komotini and Loutraki.
EXP2_DESC=Handled cash flow and finance transactions, invoices and orders; negotiated with clients and suppliers.
EXP1_DESC=Provided technical support and device repairs in Ag. Stefanos; managed sales and cash operations.

# The full company name runs into the timeline dot in the narrow print column.
EXP2_COMPANY=Zabouris - Simotas IKE

# Projects, one or two print lines each (<= 95 characters). WIFI4GR keeps its
# numbers: they are the strongest evidence on the sheet.
PROJ1_DESC=Deployed 480 Huawei firewalls and onboarded 1,000+ access points to iMaster NCE nationwide.
PROJ2_DESC=Supported three high-tech conference rooms: cameras, microphones, monitoring and AV equipment.
PROJ3_DESC=Provided outsourced IT Helpdesk support: incident management and end-user troubleshooting.

# FISH, APIS and OTDR are three small support engagements; printed as one entry
# they save about four lines. Religious Greece moves up into PROJ5, and the
# leftover PROJ6/PROJ7 are blanked: empty elements are hidden in print.
PROJ4_TITLE=FISH · APIS · OTDR
PROJ4_DESC=Public-sector tablet and passenger-control software support; ticketing for an energy company.
PROJ5_TITLE=Religious Greece
PROJ5_DESC=Supported the website and managed Acronis backups for a major religious heritage organisation.
PROJ6_TITLE=
PROJ6_DESC=
PROJ7_TITLE=
PROJ7_DESC=

# Education and certification, compressed so the sheet holds one A4 page.
EDU_DESC=Ongoing studies: computer systems, electronics and IT.
CERT1_DESC1=Covers networking, IP connectivity and services, security and automation.
